mhvtld for Debian
=================

mhvtld is installed but neither enabled nor started. To run it:

  systemctl enable --now mhvtld

It listens on http://127.0.0.1:8080 by default. Options, including the
listen address, an API token and TLS, are set in /etc/mhvtl/mhvtld.env
(mode 0600); restart mhvtld after changing it. mhvtld refuses to bind a
non-loopback address without a token.

mhvtld finds mhVTL's libraries in /etc/mhvtl/device.conf and talks to the
running mhVTL daemons, so it is useful once the mhvtl package is set up.
It tolerates mhVTL starting after it, and mhVTL restarts.
